1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,000
Το Plex ζήτησε 120€ για να συνεχίσετε να βλέπετε από τις συσκευές σας.
Το πλήρωσα εγώ το ποσό.

2
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:10,000
Αν χρησιμοποιείτε συχνά και μπορείτε,
 οποιαδήποτε συμβολή θα εκτιμηθεί.

3
00:01:37,340 --> 00:01:41,800
This area has always been
difficult to navigate,

4
00:01:41,800 --> 00:01:44,680
so all kinds of things wash up here.

5
00:01:45,930 --> 00:01:49,940
It used to be that the entire village
helped clean up the shore.

6
00:01:49,940 --> 00:01:53,020
But now you don't have enough people,
so it lies neglected.

7
00:01:53,860 --> 00:01:58,030
These waters used to be beautifully clear.

8
00:01:59,450 --> 00:02:00,610
I know.

9
00:02:03,580 --> 00:02:06,450
How about this as payment?

10
00:02:09,420 --> 00:02:12,420
It's a book written by
Flamme the Legendary Mage.

11
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:14,420
Ms. Frieren.

12
00:02:15,210 --> 00:02:17,590
Is this the only grimoire
you have in your village?

13
00:02:17,880 --> 00:02:18,760
Yes.

14
00:02:19,380 --> 00:02:23,220
Very well. We'll clean up the area for you.

15
00:02:27,470 --> 00:02:30,480
That grimoire is a fake, isn't it?

16
00:02:30,900 --> 00:02:34,820
I see you've been studying like
I told you to. Good girl, Fern.

17
00:02:35,480 --> 00:02:40,700
Books attributed to Flamme are never real.
This is just another poor imitation.

18
00:02:41,110 --> 00:02:43,070
Why did you accept the job?

19
00:02:44,070 --> 00:02:46,620
To help someone in need.

20
00:02:47,120 --> 00:02:49,500
I find that hard to believe.

21
00:02:50,920 --> 00:02:54,290
You're right. I'm doing this for me.

22
00:02:56,880 --> 00:02:59,630
Sounds like we've got another
long stay ahead of us.

23
00:03:14,900 --> 00:03:17,820
Thanks for being such a
regular customer, Fern.

24
00:03:17,820 --> 00:03:20,190
I threw in an extra one for you.

25
00:03:20,190 --> 00:03:21,900
Thank you.

26
00:03:21,900 --> 00:03:24,240
It's been three months already.

27
00:03:24,490 --> 00:03:26,280
Have you gotten used to the village?

28
00:03:26,280 --> 00:03:27,080
Yes.

29
00:03:27,080 --> 00:03:32,000
The shore gets cold this
time of year. Be careful.

30
00:03:36,210 --> 00:03:37,880
<i>It's winter already.</i>

31
00:03:43,180 --> 00:03:44,590
She's still asleep.

32
00:03:45,800 --> 00:03:47,640
This place is a mess.

33
00:03:48,140 --> 00:03:50,640
<i>I just tidied up yesterday, too.</i>

34
00:03:52,560 --> 00:03:56,400
Ms. Frieren, it's morning. Please wake up.

35
00:04:07,370 --> 00:04:09,660
Let's go clean up the shore.

36
00:04:33,770 --> 00:04:35,310
So cold...

37
00:04:37,730 --> 00:04:39,570
I've been thinking.

38
00:04:39,980 --> 00:04:41,070
About what?

39
00:04:41,440 --> 00:04:46,570
Are you actually a very sloppy person?

40
00:04:46,950 --> 00:04:52,120
Every morning I wake you up, feed you
breakfast, and help you get dressed.

41
00:04:52,830 --> 00:04:56,080
I'm practically your mother.

42
00:04:56,330 --> 00:04:58,540
I can do all that myself.

43
00:04:58,540 --> 00:05:01,710
But then you'd sleep until noon.

44
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:03,010
Yeah.

45
00:05:03,010 --> 00:05:06,090
Well, I've already given up hope, anyway.

46
00:05:06,720 --> 00:05:08,180
Sorry.

47
00:05:08,760 --> 00:05:11,970
How did you manage traveling
with the hero's party?

48
00:05:12,390 --> 00:05:15,430
There wasn't anyone there
to look after you.

49
00:05:15,430 --> 00:05:17,560
I overslept all the time.

50
00:05:18,150 --> 00:05:20,560
And you never got in trouble for it?

51
00:05:20,900 --> 00:05:23,650
I did, just once.

52
00:05:24,070 --> 00:05:29,030
Just once? They must have been very tolerant.

53
00:05:29,030 --> 00:05:30,820
They were a whole different breed.

54
00:05:31,370 --> 00:05:34,410
Also, Heiter sometimes clicked his tongue.

55
00:05:34,910 --> 00:05:35,790
Sorry.

56
00:05:36,460 --> 00:05:37,410
Hey.

57
00:05:37,410 --> 00:05:39,120
I understand how you feel, but...

58
00:05:39,580 --> 00:05:42,590
Sounds like they were rather upset with you.

59
00:05:55,270 --> 00:05:57,730
How is the cleanup coming along?

60
00:05:58,640 --> 00:06:01,230
We have about a third of it left.

61
00:06:01,730 --> 00:06:04,900
Do you think you'll be done in time
for the New Year's Festival?

62
00:06:04,900 --> 00:06:06,190
Just barely.

63
00:06:06,740 --> 00:06:13,160
In that case, I hope you'll be able to watch
the sunrise this time, Ms. Frieren.

64
00:06:21,170 --> 00:06:26,260
Is the beach cleanup related to
the New Year's Festival somehow?

65
00:06:27,090 --> 00:06:31,640
In this village, it's customary to watch the
sunrise on the day of the New Year's Festival.

66
00:06:31,890 --> 00:06:37,520
They say it's beautiful how the light
reflects off the clear waters.

67
00:06:38,140 --> 00:06:40,520
You haven't seen it?

68
00:06:41,100 --> 00:06:43,150
Do you think I'd be able
to wake up that early?

69
00:06:43,690 --> 00:06:45,650
I suppose not.

70
00:06:46,230 --> 00:06:49,110
Let's hurry. We don't have much time.

71
00:07:29,650 --> 00:07:31,950
No problems with the water quality.

72
00:07:32,320 --> 00:07:35,030
We managed to finish by the day before.

73
00:07:35,490 --> 00:07:37,780
It hardly looks like the same beach.

74
00:07:38,870 --> 00:07:41,540
Thank you, Ms. Frieren.

75
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:45,380
You'll be joining us for the
New Year's Festival, won't you?

76
00:07:45,380 --> 00:07:46,170
Yes.

77
00:07:46,460 --> 00:07:48,420
We'd love to have you.

78
00:07:49,510 --> 00:07:52,260
Have you lost your mind, Ms. Frieren?

79
00:07:52,260 --> 00:07:54,680
You'll have to wake up before the sun rises.

80
00:07:54,680 --> 00:07:56,260
That's impossible for you.

81
00:07:56,680 --> 00:07:58,930
I'll be fine. I just need
to stay up all night.

82
00:07:59,470 --> 00:08:01,930
You're that desperate to see the sunrise?

83
00:08:02,430 --> 00:08:06,940
Honestly, I'm not interested,
which is why I want to see it for myself.

84
00:08:07,980 --> 00:08:09,690
I don't understand.

85
00:08:10,190 --> 00:08:11,400
No, I suppose you wouldn't.

86
00:08:19,580 --> 00:08:23,210
Why didn't you come to the
New Year's Festival, Frieren?

87
00:08:23,660 --> 00:08:28,460
The shock was so great,
it left Heiter bedridden. Poor guy.

88
00:08:28,460 --> 00:08:31,800
He's just out of commission
because he drank too much.

89
00:08:32,260 --> 00:08:35,050
What's the problem?
The rest of you got to go.

90
00:08:35,590 --> 00:08:39,430
We wanted you to enjoy it, too.

91
00:08:39,720 --> 00:08:44,270
It's just a sunrise.
I doubt I'd enjoy it much.

92
00:08:44,270 --> 00:08:46,600
No, you would.

93
00:08:46,600 --> 00:08:47,560
Why?

94
00:08:48,610 --> 00:08:50,900
Because you're that kind of person.

95
00:08:54,780 --> 00:08:56,070
She's asleep.

96
00:08:57,780 --> 00:08:59,160
She's asleep!

97
00:08:59,160 --> 00:09:03,120
Ms. Frieren, wake up.
You'll be late for the New Year's Festival.

98
00:09:03,410 --> 00:09:04,830
Mother...

99
00:09:04,830 --> 00:09:06,580
Who are you calling "Mother"?

100
00:09:08,920 --> 00:09:11,380
Why am I doing this?

101
00:09:14,050 --> 00:09:16,590
Thank you, Fern.

102
00:09:30,150 --> 00:09:35,320
<i>It's certainly pretty, but it wasn't
worth waking up early for.</i>

103
00:09:36,240 --> 00:09:39,070
<i>Himmel didn't understand me after all.</i>

104
00:09:40,280 --> 00:09:42,580
Fern, I'm going home so I can go back to...

105
00:09:43,490 --> 00:09:47,000
Ms. Frieren, it's beautiful.

106
00:09:48,500 --> 00:09:50,000
Is it?

107
00:09:51,080 --> 00:09:52,840
It's just a sunrise.

108
00:09:54,800 --> 00:09:58,010
But you seem to be enjoying
yourself a little.

109
00:09:58,430 --> 00:10:01,930
That's because you're smiling.

110
00:10:10,520 --> 00:10:14,650
I wouldn't have been able to see
this sunrise if I'd been on my own.

111
00:10:14,650 --> 00:10:19,610
Of course not. After all, you can't
get out of bed by yourself.

112
00:10:25,580 --> 00:10:27,410
Are these for your family?

113
00:10:27,410 --> 00:10:29,500
It was a long time ago.

114
00:10:29,500 --> 00:10:33,000
My village was attacked by demons.

115
00:10:36,090 --> 00:10:37,420
What are you doing?

116
00:10:38,380 --> 00:10:39,970
Praying.

117
00:10:39,970 --> 00:10:42,930
People return to nothingness when they die.

118
00:10:42,930 --> 00:10:44,930
No, they go to Heaven.

119
00:10:45,430 --> 00:10:46,930
Until several thousand years ago,

120
00:10:46,930 --> 00:10:49,940
the commonly held belief
was that there was no afterlife.

121
00:10:50,390 --> 00:10:52,770
Dwarves value tradition.

122
00:10:53,190 --> 00:10:56,570
I'm skeptical about the idea
of a heaven myself,

123
00:10:56,570 --> 00:11:01,820
but since current magics can't
observe the souls of the dead,

124
00:11:01,820 --> 00:11:04,370
its existence can't be proven or disproven.

125
00:11:04,370 --> 00:11:06,910
I don't think it matters either way.

126
00:11:07,290 --> 00:11:11,920
You're right. I don't care
if it exists or not.

127
00:11:12,170 --> 00:11:15,420
Should a man of the cloth be saying that,
you corrupt priest?

128
00:11:15,840 --> 00:11:21,260
But even if it doesn't exist,
I believe it should.

129
00:11:21,260 --> 00:11:22,220
Why?

130
00:11:22,880 --> 00:11:25,850
Because it's more convenient that way.

131
00:11:26,390 --> 00:11:29,520
All those people doing their best
to live deserve something better

132
00:11:29,520 --> 00:11:31,770
than nothingness awaiting them.

133
00:11:32,730 --> 00:11:38,690
I prefer to think they get to
live the good life in Heaven.

134
00:11:43,740 --> 00:11:45,450
That certainly is more convenient.

135
00:11:46,030 --> 00:11:47,080
Shall we pray?

136
00:11:47,910 --> 00:11:48,660
Yeah.

137
00:12:04,470 --> 00:12:06,850
Eisen, I'm here to hang out.

138
00:12:07,600 --> 00:12:11,060
You act like it hasn't been thirty years.

139
00:12:11,640 --> 00:12:13,690
What's a mere thirty years?

140
00:12:16,100 --> 00:12:17,520
You're right.

141
00:12:18,940 --> 00:12:22,440
I never thought you'd take on an apprentice.

142
00:12:23,820 --> 00:12:27,570
Eisen, is there anything you need help with?

143
00:12:28,070 --> 00:12:33,540
Frieren, I heard you asked
Heiter the same thing.

144
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:36,210
I'm not on my deathbed yet.

145
00:12:36,710 --> 00:12:38,420
How do you know about that?

146
00:12:38,960 --> 00:12:41,210
Because we wrote to each other.

147
00:12:41,210 --> 00:12:43,590
You're more conscientious than you look.

148
00:12:43,970 --> 00:12:46,970
You're just too indifferent.

149
00:12:46,970 --> 00:12:50,760
So, do you need help with anything?

150
00:12:54,310 --> 00:12:55,850
Voll Basin...

151
00:12:56,190 --> 00:12:57,520
This place brings back memories.

152
00:12:58,190 --> 00:12:59,980
You've been here before?

153
00:12:59,980 --> 00:13:01,020
A long time ago.

154
00:13:01,730 --> 00:13:05,450
"A long time," she said.
How long must that be?

155
00:13:06,820 --> 00:13:08,740
Perhaps she came here in prehistoric times.

156
00:13:08,740 --> 00:13:11,490
Not even I've lived that long.

157
00:13:13,790 --> 00:13:16,250
So, what are we looking for?

158
00:13:16,830 --> 00:13:19,960
The notes of Flamme the Legendary Mage.

159
00:13:21,920 --> 00:13:26,510
Fine. You know most of Flamme's
supposed writings are fake, though?

160
00:13:26,840 --> 00:13:28,390
I have a lead.

161
00:13:28,890 --> 00:13:35,480
Heiter deduced the location from records
on Flamme left in the holy city.

162
00:13:36,480 --> 00:13:40,230
Her genuine notes are located
somewhere in Voll Basin.

163
00:13:41,150 --> 00:13:44,610
Frieren, you must know that.

164
00:13:45,490 --> 00:13:49,570
That corrupt priest.
He'd gotten that far in his research?

165
00:13:50,490 --> 00:13:54,200
Fine. We'll begin by searching
for a large tree.

166
00:13:54,660 --> 00:13:56,410
A large tree?

167
00:13:56,790 --> 00:14:00,080
That's ridiculous. There are tons of trees.

168
00:14:00,750 --> 00:14:04,340
Well, I suppose you have
all the time in the world.

169
00:14:04,340 --> 00:14:05,420
That's right.

170
00:14:05,960 --> 00:14:09,430
But Fern wouldn't like that,
so I'll try to finish quickly.

171
00:14:12,930 --> 00:14:15,430
Let's search as efficiently as possible.

172
00:14:18,060 --> 00:14:19,520
You've changed.

173
00:14:20,520 --> 00:14:24,480
You never cared about
other people's time before.

174
00:14:25,070 --> 00:14:27,900
Fern is scary when she's mad.

175
00:14:29,150 --> 00:14:31,780
I see. Then I should watch myself.

176
00:15:05,520 --> 00:15:06,820
Ms. Frieren.

177
00:15:07,480 --> 00:15:11,110
There's a large tree to the west
growing over some ruins.

178
00:15:11,990 --> 00:15:13,030
This way.

179
00:15:13,660 --> 00:15:14,870
Got it.

180
00:15:17,950 --> 00:15:22,500
Hey. Why did you decide to
look for Flamme's notes?

181
00:15:23,540 --> 00:15:25,840
Because I felt sorry for you.

182
00:15:26,250 --> 00:15:27,170
What?

183
00:15:27,590 --> 00:15:31,800
I felt sorry for you and Himmel.

184
00:15:32,590 --> 00:15:34,840
On that day thirty years ago,

185
00:15:34,840 --> 00:15:38,810
you said you wished you'd gotten
to know Himmel better.

186
00:15:39,350 --> 00:15:44,060
You should tell Himmel himself that.

187
00:15:45,440 --> 00:15:52,950
They say the notes of Flamme the Legendary
Mage describe her conversing with the dead.

188
00:15:53,280 --> 00:15:58,200
That's just a fairy tale.
Besides, I don't want to see him now.

189
00:15:58,490 --> 00:16:02,040
All magic started as fairy tales.

190
00:16:02,500 --> 00:16:05,630
And don't you want to know more about Himmel?

191
00:16:06,710 --> 00:16:09,590
That's why I talked it over with Heiter.

192
00:16:09,880 --> 00:16:15,840
We were sure you had regrets,
so we wanted to help you.

193
00:16:24,850 --> 00:16:30,360
Ms. Frieren, both the tree and ruins
are protected by a powerful barrier.

194
00:16:33,190 --> 00:16:39,330
Even after a thousand years, I'm still
dancing in the palm of my master's hand.

195
00:16:41,620 --> 00:16:44,250
How's that little sapling going to keep watch?

196
00:16:44,250 --> 00:16:45,830
Don't sell it short.

197
00:16:47,630 --> 00:16:52,630
Once it grows, it'll still be protecting
this place a thousand years from now.

198
00:16:53,090 --> 00:16:55,630
You'll be dead by then.

199
00:16:57,180 --> 00:16:58,930
But you won't be.

200
00:16:59,300 --> 00:17:05,270
Someday, you'll make a terrible mistake
and wish you'd gotten to know people better.

201
00:17:05,640 --> 00:17:09,150
Do you wish I knew you better?
Are you being needy?

202
00:17:09,150 --> 00:17:10,570
Yeah, no.

203
00:17:10,900 --> 00:17:13,900
When that happens, return to this place.

204
00:17:14,690 --> 00:17:20,030
Then I, Flamme the Legendary Mage,
will help you.

205
00:17:34,920 --> 00:17:37,300
Those are Flamme's notes?

206
00:17:38,680 --> 00:17:40,390
Are they real?

207
00:17:40,800 --> 00:17:42,260
They're real.

208
00:17:42,680 --> 00:17:44,270
How do you know that?

209
00:17:44,770 --> 00:17:47,810
Frieren was Flamme's best student.

210
00:17:48,440 --> 00:17:53,900
Flamme the Legendary Mage is an ancient hero
who's written about in magical history.

211
00:17:54,900 --> 00:17:57,780
Are you sure you haven't been
around since prehistoric times?

212
00:17:58,200 --> 00:18:01,320
Does it say anything about
speaking to the dead?

213
00:18:01,780 --> 00:18:04,790
It's already opened to that very page.

214
00:18:05,620 --> 00:18:10,000
Did she know a thousand years ago
that I'd come here?

215
00:18:10,580 --> 00:18:13,130
What an unpleasant woman.

216
00:18:14,170 --> 00:18:16,840
"On the northernmost end of the continent..."

217
00:18:17,510 --> 00:18:21,090
<i>I arrived at the place the people
of this world call heaven:</i>

218
00:18:21,590 --> 00:18:25,470
<i>Aureole, the land where souls rest.</i>

219
00:18:26,140 --> 00:18:29,100
<i>Many souls gather there,</i>

220
00:18:29,560 --> 00:18:32,650
<i>and I spoke with friends
who once fought alongside me.</i>

221
00:18:34,690 --> 00:18:37,110
<i>This discovery of the century...</i>

222
00:18:37,110 --> 00:18:40,780
"... will propel research on souls forward."

223
00:18:42,740 --> 00:18:44,870
Do you suppose it's true?

224
00:18:44,870 --> 00:18:48,040
Who knows? She was an irresponsible person.

225
00:18:48,580 --> 00:18:50,210
Heaven exists.

226
00:18:50,750 --> 00:18:53,710
It's more convenient if it does.

227
00:18:55,040 --> 00:18:59,090
You're right. Perhaps I should
believe in it for once.

228
00:19:00,260 --> 00:19:03,220
Where exactly is this place?

229
00:19:03,640 --> 00:19:05,100
Give me a moment.

230
00:19:05,930 --> 00:19:09,100
The northern continent... Ende.

231
00:19:09,770 --> 00:19:11,140
Ende?

232
00:19:11,140 --> 00:19:12,100
Yes.

233
00:19:13,730 --> 00:19:16,230
It's where the Demon King's
castle is located now.

234
00:19:18,530 --> 00:19:20,360
But why there?

235
00:19:21,150 --> 00:19:22,360
Frieren.

236
00:19:22,990 --> 00:19:27,120
You must find Aureole and speak with Himmel.

237
00:19:29,580 --> 00:19:32,000
You said you'd help me, didn't you?

238
00:19:34,250 --> 00:19:37,000
You've learned some cunning tricks, Eisen.

239
00:19:37,670 --> 00:19:39,670
Thanks to Heiter.

240
00:19:40,510 --> 00:19:43,930
Fine. I didn't have a particular
destination anyway.

241
00:19:45,220 --> 00:19:49,350
But it's so cold around
the Demon King's castle.

242
00:19:50,310 --> 00:19:52,350
I don't want to go.

243
00:19:52,940 --> 00:19:55,650
She's already feeling discouraged.

244
00:20:00,740 --> 00:20:02,650
She fell asleep.

245
00:20:02,650 --> 00:20:04,450
What a carefree girl.

246
00:20:05,700 --> 00:20:08,950
It's cold. I don't want to go.

247
00:20:08,950 --> 00:20:10,200
She's moaning in her sleep.

248
00:20:10,870 --> 00:20:14,080
Is it really that cold around
the Demon King's castle?

249
00:20:17,670 --> 00:20:23,220
Ende, where the castle is, is located at the
very northernmost end of the continent.

250
00:20:23,680 --> 00:20:27,180
We went through a lot in that place.

251
00:20:28,140 --> 00:20:29,350
A lot?

252
00:20:36,480 --> 00:20:38,560
<i>This is awkward.</i>

253
00:20:39,650 --> 00:20:42,150
<i>Maybe I'll wake Ms. Frieren.</i>

254
00:20:43,570 --> 00:20:46,410
Ms. Frieren. Ms. Frieren.

255
00:20:49,330 --> 00:20:51,200
She won't wake up.

256
00:20:51,700 --> 00:20:56,580
Say, Fern. Is she a good master?

257
00:20:57,500 --> 00:20:58,880
That's a good question.

258
00:20:59,340 --> 00:21:01,050
I don't really know.

259
00:21:01,670 --> 00:21:06,970
All she does is drag me around
while she searches for magic.

260
00:21:08,220 --> 00:21:14,020
But she does seem interested in getting
to know Mr. Himmel and his companions.

261
00:21:15,230 --> 00:21:19,560
Perhaps she's not very interested in me.

262
00:21:20,480 --> 00:21:23,280
Ms. Frieren only took me on as an apprentice

263
00:21:24,070 --> 00:21:26,900
because she promised Mr. Heiter she would.

264
00:21:28,780 --> 00:21:29,820
I see.

265
00:21:30,870 --> 00:21:34,120
But she's such a strange person.

266
00:21:34,620 --> 00:21:39,920
After we began traveling together,
she started giving me birthday presents.

267
00:21:40,630 --> 00:21:42,920
Normally she seems so disinterested in me.

268
00:21:44,510 --> 00:21:48,680
I wonder what she's thinking.
She's so strange.

269
00:21:54,220 --> 00:21:57,640
Frieren, you're not going
to stay in the royal capital?

270
00:21:58,310 --> 00:22:00,100
I'm going to keep traveling.

271
00:22:00,100 --> 00:22:01,560
Alone?

272
00:22:01,560 --> 00:22:03,110
It'll be nice and easy.

273
00:22:03,860 --> 00:22:06,280
You're not going to take on an apprentice?

274
00:22:06,280 --> 00:22:09,200
Traveling is better when you
have someone to talk to.

275
00:22:09,570 --> 00:22:11,870
It's a waste of time.

276
00:22:11,870 --> 00:22:14,700
Even if I taught them, they'd die in no time.

277
00:22:17,330 --> 00:22:21,580
Frieren, that's not how relationships work.

278
00:22:21,960 --> 00:22:23,920
Yes, it is.

279
00:22:23,920 --> 00:22:29,050
My adventure with you wasn't even
one one-hundredth of my life.

280
00:22:29,800 --> 00:22:31,590
You must understand that, Eisen.

281
00:22:31,590 --> 00:22:33,140
I...

282
00:22:35,260 --> 00:22:38,350
Okay, okay. That's enough depressing talk.

283
00:22:38,350 --> 00:22:42,060
Today is a day for celebrating. Let's drink.

284
00:22:42,060 --> 00:22:45,070
You just want a reason to drink, don't you?

285
00:22:45,070 --> 00:22:46,610
You saw right through me.

286
00:22:46,610 --> 00:22:49,200
You're always drinking.

287
00:22:49,200 --> 00:22:50,860
You corrupt priest.

288
00:22:55,660 --> 00:22:56,490
Fern...

289
00:22:57,330 --> 00:23:00,000
She's a good master.

290
00:23:02,580 --> 00:23:03,920
You're right.

291
00:23:08,460 --> 00:23:10,800
Eisen, you're really not coming with us?

292
00:23:11,260 --> 00:23:12,260
That's right.

293
00:23:12,590 --> 00:23:17,010
I told you before, I'd only get in your way.

294
00:23:18,180 --> 00:23:19,270
I see.

295
00:23:19,640 --> 00:23:23,440
You remember how to get to Ende, don't you?

296
00:23:23,440 --> 00:23:26,150
Yes. First we travel through the Wille region,

297
00:23:26,150 --> 00:23:30,280
and then we cross Riegel Canyon and pass
through the northern lands checkpoint.

298
00:23:32,570 --> 00:23:33,910
Sorry to ask this of you.

299
00:23:34,320 --> 00:23:36,280
It'll be a long journey.

300
00:23:36,910 --> 00:23:39,750
It took us ten years.

301
00:23:41,870 --> 00:23:43,120
I see.

302
00:23:43,120 --> 00:23:47,880
We'll be following the same path Mr. Himmel's
party took to the Demon King's castle.

303
00:24:14,410 --> 00:24:15,620
You're right.

304
00:24:16,410 --> 00:24:18,700
It'll be a mere ten-year adventure.

305
00:25:50,250 --> 00:25:52,460
Do you think I can become a powerful warrior?

306
00:25:51,000 --> 00:25:53,170
They appear after death.

307
00:25:51,420 --> 00:25:54,800
You really do only collect odd spells.

308
00:25:52,460 --> 00:25:55,920
Travelers, may I have a moment of your time?

309
00:25:53,960 --> 00:25:55,920
Why haven't you defeated the dragon?

310
00:25:55,920 --> 00:25:57,800
You're searching for it, aren't you?

311
00:25:56,550 --> 00:25:57,800
That's ridiculous.

312
00:25:57,800 --> 00:25:59,890
This is a phantom of the dead.
